---
description: 
globs: *.llm.mdx
alwaysApply: false
---
(extract-components) When asked to refactor styled components from a page.tsx:

1. Identify visually distinct sections with their own styling (cards, hero sections, feature grids, etc.)
2. Extract each section into a separate component file in `src/components`
3. Component names should be descriptive and PascalCase (e.g., `HeroSection`, `FeatureCard`, `CallToAction`)
4. Components should take no props initially - they should be self-contained with their content and styling
5. Use proper TypeScript and include all necessary imports
6. Replace the original page.tsx sections with the new component imports

(mdx-markup) After extracting components, update the corresponding `.llm.mdx` file:
1. Wrap relevant content sections with semantic markers: `<ComponentName>content</ComponentName>`
2. The content inside markers should be the original MDX text that describes what the component represents
3. Marker names should exactly match the extracted component names
4. Preserve the original MDX structure and hierarchy
5. Add comments above markers to explain the component's purpose: `<!-- HeroSection: Main landing area with title and CTA -->`

(sync-content) Ensure the MDX markers and TSX components stay synchronized:
- MDX content inside markers describes the semantic meaning
- TSX components implement the visual representation
- Changes to either should be reflected in both files
- Use the marker content as the source of truth for component text content

Example transformation:
MDX: `# Welcome to Our Platform` → `{/* HeroSection: Main landing area */}\n<HeroSection>\n# Welcome to Our Platform\n</HeroSection>`
TSX: Extract hero styling into `src/components/HeroSection.tsx` and import in page.tsx 